mode: "100644"
text: "# The CHAIN framework — build every video as a link, not an island\n\nLong-form is the opposite of Shorts: no swipe to win, but a **packaging gate** (the click) and a\n**retention gate** (do they stay — and watch more). And the dominant 2026 signal isn't your\nvideo's watch time, it's whether your video makes the **session** longer. So build each upload as\na link in a CHAIN.\n\n## C — Click (packaging earns the impression → CTR)\n- **Package before you produce.** Write the title and sketch the thumbnail *before* scripting. If\n  you can't make the packaging compelling, the idea isn't strong enough yet.\n- **Clarity beats clickbait beats clutter.** The fastest CTR lifts usually come from *removing*\n  clutter — one clear idea, readable at mobile size, accurate to the video.\n- **A/B test** title/thumbnail variants in Studio. Target a healthy niche CTR (~4–10%).\n\n## H — Hook (the first 30 seconds pay off the promise)\n- **Open with the payoff, the stakes, or the question.** No logo animation, no \"hey guys.\"\n- Deliver *exactly* what the packaging promised, immediately. A steep early drop is read as\n  clickbait-that-didn't-deliver and chokes distribution. (Lines → hook-writer.)\n\n## A — AVD (structure holds retention)\n- **Re-hook every 60–90 seconds:** open loops, pattern interrupts, B-roll, angle/tone changes.\n- **One topic, no padding.** Match length to the idea (8–15 min when retention holds). Cutting\n  length is often the strongest single fix.\n- Watch the retention curve for the cliffs and fix those specific moments.\n\n## I — Iterate (diagnose with three numbers)\n- **CTR** = packaging. **30-sec retention** = hook. **AVD %** = structure. These three tell you\n  exactly what to fix next.\n- **Test one variable at a time** (hook, then thumbnail, then topic, then timing). Intentional\n  testers grow markedly faster than random posters. Improve one element per upload.\n\n## N — Next (engineer session contribution — the dominant signal)\n- End every video by **chaining to the next watch**: a specific end-screen video, a playlist, a\n  series with clear progression, a \"watch next\" that continues the session.\n- Make the next-video watch time *high* — if viewers bounce off your end screen, you're killing\n  sessions. Pick the chain target deliberately.\n- **Bridge from Shorts:** each Short should reference a specific long-form (the click-through is\n  tracked). The chain spans formats. (Sibling: youtube-shorts.)\n\n## The blueprint a plan should fill\n```\nPACKAGE   working title + thumbnail concept (before script)\nCOLD OPEN  payoff/stakes in the first 30s, matches the package\nBODY       segmented value, re-hook every 60–90s, no padding, target length\nCLOSE      single CTA + an explicit NEXT (end screen / playlist / series)\nSHIP WITH  keyword-aligned description + chapters (Search), captions,\n           Altered-Content disclosure if AI-generated\n```\n"
